{"id": "release-code-toposort", "kind": "code", "family": "toposort", "passed": false, "reason": "execution or assertion failure", "text": "```python\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\n\ndef toposort(graph: dict) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Return a valid topological ordering of nodes in the graph.\n    graph: a dict mapping a node to its dependencies (list of nodes that must come before it).\n    Returns: a list of nodes such that for every dependency d of n, d appears before n.\n    Raises: ValueError if a cycle is detected.\n    \"\"\"\n    visited = set()\n    rec_stack = set()\n    result = []\n\n    def dfs(node):\n        if node in rec_stack:\n            raise ValueError(\"Cycle detected in the graph\")\n        if node in visited:\n            return\n\n        visited.add(node)\n        rec_stack.add(node)\n\n        for dep in graph.get(node, []):\n            if dep not in visited:\n                dfs(dep)\n\n        rec_stack.remove(node)\n        result.append(node)\n\n    # Ensure all nodes in the graph are processed\n    all_nodes = set(graph.keys())\n    for deps in graph.values():\n        all_nodes.update(deps)\n\n    for node in all_nodes:\n        if node not in visited:\n            dfs(node)\n\n    return result\n```", "tool_calls": [], "finish_reason": "stop", "input_tokens": 75, "output_tokens": 261, "seconds": 3.447, "tokens_per_second": 83.0, "peak_memory_gb": 3.667}
